# Shell scripts must use LF line endings.
#
# A CRLF checked-out script makes bash parse "set -euo pipefail\r" and fail with
# "set: pipefail: invalid option name", because the carriage return becomes part
# of the option name. The eol=lf attribute overrides core.autocrlf on checkout,
# so every machine gets LF regardless of its Git line-ending settings.
*.sh text eol=lf
